* text=auto eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.csv text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.cpp text eol=lf
*.hpp text eol=lf
*.h text eol=lf
*.c text eol=lf
# External library sources (<root>/<Lib>/<lib>-<version>/, where the roots are Core/Source/ThirdParty and Engine/Source/ThirdParty) are kept
# byte for byte (no line ending conversion). Each library's ThirdParty.json verifies them with per-file SHA-256. Rocks glue lives directly under <Lib>/
# and is outside this rule.
Core/Source/ThirdParty/*/*/** -text
Engine/Source/ThirdParty/*/*/** -text
# Patches of traceable modifications keep LF as is (ThirdPartyPatch rejects CR, and context line bytes must match the source).
Core/Source/ThirdParty/*/*.patch text eol=lf
Engine/Source/ThirdParty/*/*.patch text eol=lf
# Offline tool build scripts and patches of prebuilt binaries (<Lib>/Build/) are written by Rocks, so they are excluded from the source rule (later rules win).
Engine/Source/ThirdParty/*/Build/** text eol=lf
*.pdf binary
*.png binary
*.zip binary
# Unreal exchange bundle blobs are named by the SHA-256 of their bytes (Docs/Design/UnrealExchange.ko.md section 3.1), so they are kept byte for byte.
**/*.rxbundle/blobs/** binary
